      "explanation": "When multiplying a 3\u00d74 matrix by a 4\u00d72 matrix, the resulting matrix has order 3\u00d72."
    },
    {
      "id": "MATH_24_02",
      "topic": "Relations and Functions",
      "sub_topic": "Domain and Range",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "question": "The domain of the function f(x) = \u221a(x\u00b2 - 16) is:",
      "options": [
        "A) [-4, 4]",
        "B) [0, \u221e)",
        "C) (-\u221e, 4]",
        "D) (-\u221e, -4] \u222a [4, \u221e)"
      ],
      "correct_option": "D",
      "explanation": "x\u00b2 - 16 \u2265 0 \u2192 x\u00b2 \u2265 16 \u2192 x \u2264 -4 or x \u2265 4. Domain: (-\u221e, -4] \u222a [4, \u221e)."
    },
    {
      "id": "P24_03",
      "topic": "Algebra",
      "sub_topic": "Probability",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "question": "A bag contains 5 red balls and 7 blue balls. If one ball is drawn at random, what is the probability that it is red?",
      "options": [
        "A) 5/7",
        "B) 5/12",
        "C) 1/2",
        "D) 7/12"
      ],
      "correct_option": "B",
      "explanation": "Total balls = 5 + 7 = 12. Favorable outcomes (red) = 5. Probability = 5/12."
    },
    {
      "id": "P24_04",
      "topic": "Algebra",
      "sub_topic": "Integration",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "question": "The value of \u222b(3x\u00b2 + 2x + 1) dx is:",
      "options": [
        "A) x\u00b3 + x\u00b2 + C",
        "B) x\u00b3 + x\u00b2 + x + C",
        "C) 6x + 2 + C",
        "D) 3x\u00b3 + 2x\u00b2 + x + C"
      ],
      "correct_option": "B",
      "explanation": "\u222b(3x\u00b2 + 2x + 1) dx = 3(x\u00b3/3) + 2(x\u00b2/2) + x + C = x\u00b3 + x\u00b2 + x + C."
    },
    {
      "id": "MATH_24_05",
      "topic": "Relations and Functions",
      "sub_topic": "Inverse Trigonometric Functions",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "question": "The value of sin\u207b\u00b9(1/2) + sin\u207b\u00b9(1/2) is:",
      "options": [
        "A) \u03c0/3",
        "B) \u03c0/4",
        "C) \u03c0/2",
        "D) \u03c0/6"
      ],
      "correct_option": "A",
      "explanation": "sin\u207b\u00b9(1/2) = \u03c0/6. So sin\u207b\u00b9(1/2) + sin\u207b\u00b9(1/2) = \u03c0/6 + \u03c0/6 = \u03c0/3."
    },
    {
      "id": "P24_06",
      "topic": "Algebra",
      "sub_topic": "Determinants",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "question": "If A = [[2, 3], [1, 4]], then |A| equals:",
      "options": [
        "A) 8",
        "B) 2",
        "C) 11",
        "D) 5"
      ],
      "correct_option": "D",
      "explanation": "|A| = (2)(4) - (3)(1) = 8 - 3 = 5."
    },
    {
      "id": "MATH_24_07",
      "topic": "Algebra",
      "sub_topic": "Linear Programming",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "question": "In a linear programming problem, the optimal solution is found:",
      "options": [
        "A) At a vertex of the feasible region",
        "B) At the origin",
        "C) Outside the feasible region",
        "D) On the boundary only"
      ],
      "correct_option": "A",
      "explanation": "The optimal solution in linear programming is always found at a vertex (corner point) of the feasible region."
    },
    {
      "id": "P24_08",
      "topic": "Applied Mathematics",
      "sub_topic": "Financial Mathematics",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "question": "A sum of \u20b95000 amounts to \u20b96500 in 3 years at simple interest. The rate of interest per annum is:",
      "options": [
        "A) 10%",
        "B) 15%",
        "C) 8%",
        "D) 12%"
      ],
      "correct_option": "A",
      "explanation": "SI = 6500 - 5000 = 1500. Using SI = P\u00d7R\u00d7T/100: 1500 = 5000\u00d7R\u00d73/100, so R = (1500\u00d7100)/(5000\u00d73) = 10%."
    },
    {
      "id": "P24_09",
      "topic": "Algebra",
      "sub_topic": "Matrices",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "If A = [[1, 2], [3, 4]], then A\u207b\u00b9 is:",
      "options": [
        "A) (-1/2)[[4, 2], [3, 1]]",
        "B) (1/2)[[4, -2], [-3, 1]]",
        "C) (-1/2)[[1, -2], [-3, 4]]",
        "D) (-1/2)[[4, -2], [-3, 1]]"
      ],
      "correct_option": "D",
      "explanation": "|A| = 1\u00d74 - 2\u00d73 = -2. Adjoint of A = [[4, -2], [-3, 1]]. So A\u207b\u00b9 = adj(A)/|A| = (-1/2)[[4, -2], [-3, 1]]."
    },
    {
      "id": "P24_10",
      "topic": "Algebra",
      "sub_topic": "Calculus",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "If y = x\u00b3 sin(x), then dy/dx at x = \u03c0 is:",
      "options": [
        "A) 3\u03c0\u00b2",
        "B) -3\u03c0\u00b2",
        "C) -\u03c0\u00b3",
        "D) \u03c0\u00b3"
      ],
      "correct_option": "C",
      "explanation": "dy/dx = 3x\u00b2 sin(x) + x\u00b3 cos(x). At x = \u03c0: 3\u03c0\u00b2 sin(\u03c0) + \u03c0\u00b3 cos(\u03c0) = 3\u03c0\u00b2(0) + \u03c0\u00b3(-1) = -\u03c0\u00b3."
    },
    {
      "id": "P24_11",
      "topic": "Algebra",
      "sub_topic": "Probability",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "A die is thrown twice. Let A be the event that the first throw is 6, and B be the event that the sum is 8. What is P(A\u2229B)?",
      "options": [
        "A) 1/6",
        "B) 5/36",
        "C) 1/12",
        "D) 1/36"
      ],
      "correct_option": "D",
      "explanation": "A\u2229B occurs when first throw is 6 AND sum is 8, so second throw must be 2. Only outcome: (6,2). P(A\u2229B) = 1/36."
    },
    {
      "id": "P24_12",
      "topic": "Algebra",
      "sub_topic": "Integration",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "The value of \u222b\u2080\u00b9 x\u00b7e\u02e3 dx is:",
      "options": [
        "A) 1",
        "B) e",
        "C) e + 1",
        "D) e - 1"
      ],
      "correct_option": "A",
      "explanation": "Using integration by parts with u = x, dv = e\u02e3 dx: \u222bx\u00b7e\u02e3 dx = x\u00b7e\u02e3 - e\u02e3. Evaluating from 0 to 1: [x\u00b7e\u02e3 - e\u02e3]\u2080\u00b9 = (1\u00b7e - e) - (0 - 1) = 0 + 1 = 1."
    },
    {
      "id": "P24_13",
      "topic": "Algebra",
      "sub_topic": "Differential Equations",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "The order and degree of the differential equation d\u00b3y/dx\u00b3 + (d\u00b2y/dx\u00b2)\u2074 + y = 0 are respectively:",
      "options": [
        "A) 2 and 4",
        "B) 3 and 1",
        "C) 3 and 4",
        "D) 1 and 3"
      ],
      "correct_option": "B",
      "explanation": "The highest derivative is d\u00b3y/dx\u00b3, so order = 3. The degree is the power of the highest derivative, which is 1."
    },
    {
      "id": "P24_14",
      "topic": "Relations and Functions",
      "sub_topic": "Composition of Functions",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "If f(x) = 2x + 3 and g(x) = x\u00b2 - 1, then (f\u2218g)(2) equals:",
      "options": [
        "A) 11",
        "B) 5",
        "C) 9",
        "D) 7"
      ],
      "correct_option": "C",
      "explanation": "g(2) = 2\u00b2 - 1 = 3. Then f(g(2)) = f(3) = 2(3) + 3 = 9."
    },
    {
      "id": "P24_15",
      "topic": "Relations and Functions",
      "sub_topic": "Inverse Trigonometric Functions",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "If tan\u207b\u00b9(x) + tan\u207b\u00b9(2x) = \u03c0/4, then x equals:",
      "options": [
        "A) (3 + \u221a17)/4",
        "B) (-3 + \u221a17)/4",
        "C) 1/2",
        "D) (-3 - \u221a17)/4"
      ],
      "correct_option": "B",
      "explanation": "Using tan\u207b\u00b9(a) + tan\u207b\u00b9(b) = tan\u207b\u00b9((a+b)/(1-ab)): tan\u207b\u00b9(3x/(1-2x\u00b2)) = \u03c0/4. So 3x/(1-2x\u00b2) = 1, giving 2x\u00b2 + 3x - 1 = 0. By quadratic formula: x = (-3 \u00b1 \u221a17)/4. Since ab = 2x\u00b2 < 1, we need x = (-3 + \u221a17)/4."
    },
    {
      "id": "P24_16",
      "topic": "Algebra",
      "sub_topic": "Determinants",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "If A = [[1, 2, 3], [0, 1, 4], [5, 6, 0]], then |A| equals:",
      "options": [
        "A) 2",
        "B) 0",
        "C) 1",
        "D) -1"
      ],
      "correct_option": "C",
      "explanation": "Expanding along first row: |A| = 1(1\u00b70 - 4\u00b76) - 2(0\u00b70 - 4\u00b75) + 3(0\u00b76 - 1\u00b75) = 1(-24) - 2(-20) + 3(-5) = -24 + 40 - 15 = 1."
    },
    {
      "id": "P24_17",
      "topic": "Algebra",
      "sub_topic": "Calculus",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "The maximum value of the function f(x) = x\u00b7e\u207b\u02e3 for x > 0 is:",
      "options": [
        "A) 2/e",
        "B) e",
        "C) 1",
        "D) 1/e"
      ],
      "correct_option": "D",
      "explanation": "f'(x) = e\u207b\u02e3 - x\u00b7e\u207b\u02e3 = e\u207b\u02e3(1-x). Setting f'(x) = 0 gives x = 1. f''(x) = e\u207b\u02e3(x-2). At x=1, f''(1) = -1/e < 0, so maximum. f(1) = 1\u00b7e\u207b\u00b9 = 1/e."
    },
    {
      "id": "P24_18",
      "topic": "Algebra",
      "sub_topic": "Probability",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "A box contains 4 red and 6 blue balls. Two balls are drawn without replacement. What is the probability that the second ball is red given that the first was blue?",
      "options": [
        "A) 4/9",
        "B) 4/10",
        "C) 2/5",
        "D) 6/10"
      ],
      "correct_option": "A",
      "explanation": "After drawing a blue ball first, 4 red and 5 blue remain (9 total). P(second is red | first was blue) = 4/9."
    },
    {
      "id": "P24_19",
      "topic": "Algebra",
      "sub_topic": "Integration",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "The value of \u222b\u2080^(\u03c0/2) sin\u00b2(x) dx is:",
      "options": [
        "A) \u03c0/4",
        "B) 1",
        "C) \u03c0/8",
        "D) \u03c0/2"
      ],
      "correct_option": "A",
      "explanation": "Using sin\u00b2(x) = (1 - cos(2x))/2: \u222b\u2080^(\u03c0/2) sin\u00b2(x) dx = \u222b\u2080^(\u03c0/2) (1-cos(2x))/2 dx = [x/2 - sin(2x)/4]\u2080^(\u03c0/2) = (\u03c0/4 - 0) - (0 - 0) = \u03c0/4."
    },
