    {
      "id": "P24_21",
      "topic": "Applied Mathematics",
      "sub_topic": "Numbers and Quantification",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "The remainder when 7\u00b9\u2070\u2070 is divided by 5 is:",
      "options": [
        "A) 4",
        "B) 1",
        "C) 2",
        "D) 3"
      ],
      "correct_option": "B",
      "explanation": "7 \u2261 2 (mod 5). So 7\u00b9\u2070\u2070 \u2261 2\u00b9\u2070\u2070 (mod 5). Since 2\u2074 = 16 \u2261 1 (mod 5), we have 2\u00b9\u2070\u2070 = (2\u2074)\u00b2\u2075 \u2261 1\u00b2\u2075 = 1 (mod 5). Remainder = 1."
    },
    {
      "id": "P24_22",
      "topic": "Applied Mathematics",
      "sub_topic": "Algebra",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "If the sum of the roots of x\u00b2 + px + q = 0 is 5 and the product is 6, then p and q are:",
      "options": [
        "A) p = -5, q = -6",
        "B) p = 5, q = 6",
        "C) p = -5, q = 6",
        "D) p = 5, q = -6"
      ],
      "correct_option": "C",
      "explanation": "For ax\u00b2 + bx + c = 0, sum of roots = -b/a and product = c/a. Here: -p/1 = 5, so p = -5. And q/1 = 6, so q = 6."
